- How would you adapt the model for varying delivery durations across networks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate CKNE into practical throughput controls, buffering, and shard assignment in a real pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-throughput mapping and floor guarantees
- Per-tenant buffering and backpressure
- Dynamic shard/partition weighting and rebalancing cadence
- Observability and safety checks (baseline SLA enforcement)

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeQuota(ckne, baseRate) {
  const rate = Math.max(baseRate, baseRate * (1 + 0.8 * ckne));
  const buffer = Math.ceil((1 - ckne) * 100);
  const shardWeight = ckne;
  return { rate, buffer, shardWeight };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rebalancing for fairness across tenants with identical CKNE values?
- What telemetry would you collect to verify SLA adherence during spikes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-hop, CKNE-aware backpressure and fairness across thousands of tenants with SLA-based tuning.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health as a control signal for fan-out
- Per-tenant token bucket and dynamic scaling
- SLA-tier influences on limits and queuing
- Edge backpressure signaling and aggregation
- Payload schemas and end-to-end test plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeLimit(health, queueLen, sla) {
  const base = 1000;
  if (health > 0.8 && queueLen < sla.maxQueue * 0.7) return Math.min(base * 5, sla.maxCap);
  if (health < 0.4 || queueLen > sla.maxQueue * 0.9) return Math.max(base * 0.2, sla.minCap);
  return base;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant dynamic routing with CKNE-driven SLAs, including control-plane updates and real-world observability needs.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-routing-weight mapping and fallback behavior
- Per-tenant retry budgets and deadline skew
- Dynamic metadata in Envoy and hot-reloadable config
- Validation via controlled load tests and metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
function mapCKNE(ckne){
  const primary = 0.5 + 0.5 * ckne;
  const secondary = 1 - primary;
  const retryBudget = Math.min(1 + 2 * ckne, 5);
  const deadlineSkewMs = (1 - ckne) * 50;
  return {primary, secondary, retryBudget, deadlineSkewMs};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle CKNE drift across tenants during peak hours?
- What metrics validate correctness of routing and SLA guarantees?

